fewer opportunities reduces the amount of

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:34.670
regret that one might feel.

00:12:34.670 --> 00:12:40.880
Speaker 4: Yes, although opportunity is also
an opportunity is a little bit paradoxical,

00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:44.750
so let me give you let me give you a piece
of data on that from the quantitative survey

00:12:44.750 --> 00:12:48.050
of the American Regrette Project, the big
public opinion poll.

00:12:48.050 --> 00:12:53.339
What we found there was that people who had
high levels of formal education, that is,

00:12:53.339 --> 00:12:55.730
they had degrees in advanced degrees, right?

00:12:55.730 --> 00:13:00.940
Those people we know, which is which is a
minority of of of Americans, I think it's

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:06.020
something like 30 percent or so of Americans
have a college degree and an even smaller

00:13:06.020 --> 00:13:08.870
percentage of that have a so-called advanced
